## 7️⃣ Front‑end Details {#frontend-details}
### Entry point (`client/src/index.js`)
```js
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';
import App from './App';
ReactDOM.render(<App />, document.getElementById('root'));
```
### Routing (Reach Router)
```jsx
<Router>
  <Home path="/" />
  <TopTracks path="/top-tracks" />
  <Recommendations path="/recommendations" />
  <Callback path="/callback" />
</Router>
```
### Token handling (`Callback` component)
- Parse `window.location.hash` → `access_token` & `refresh_token`.
- Store them in a **React context** (`AuthContext`).
- Redirect to the main dashboard.
### API wrapper (`client/src/spotify/index.js`)
```js
export const getTopTracks = async token => {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.spotify.com/v1/me/top/tracks?limit=20', {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
  });
  return await res.json();
};
```
### UI components (selected)
- **`TrackItem.js`** – Grid layout, hover overlay with info icon, duration formatting (`formatDuration`).
- **`TopTracks.js`** – Calls `getTopTracks`, shows a loading spinner, maps each item to `<TrackItem>`.
- **`FeatureChart.js`** – Uses Chart.js (or Recharts) to plot audio‑features like danceability, energy, etc.
- **`Recommendations.js`** – Sends seed artists/tracks to Spotify’s recommendations endpoint and renders the result.
- **`Playlist.js`** – Lists user playlists and allows selection for deeper analysis.
