## 9️⃣ Running Locally {#running-locally}
```bash
# 1️⃣ Install Node (>=10.13) – use nvm if needed
nvm use

# 2️⃣ Install dependencies for server & client
yarn && yarn client:install   # installs root + client packages

# 3️⃣ Create .env (copy from .env.example)
cp .env.example .env
#   Fill in CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET (from Spotify developer dashboard)
#   Keep REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8888/callback
#   FRONTEND_URI=http://localhost:3000

# 4️⃣ Start development servers (concurrently)
yarn dev   # runs server on 8888 and client on 3000

# 5️⃣ Open http://localhost:3000, click "Login", follow the Spotify flow.
```
### Expected output
- After login you see a dashboard with **Top Tracks**, **Audio Feature Charts**, and **Recommendations**.
