## 🔟 Deploying to Heroku {#deploying-to-heroku}
1️⃣ Create a new Heroku app: `heroku create my‑spotify‑profile`
2️⃣ Set config vars (same as .env):
```bash
heroku config:set CLIENT_ID=xxxxx CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxx REDIRECT_URI=https://my‑spotify‑profile.herokuapp.com/callback FRONTEND_URI=https://my‑spotify‑profile.herokuapp.com
```
3️⃣ Push the repo: `git push heroku master`
4️⃣ Heroku runs the `heroku-postbuild` script (`yarn && yarn client && yarn build`) which compiles the React app into `client/build` and the server serves it.
5️⃣ Visit `https://my‑spotify‑profile.herokuapp.com` – the full app works just like the local version.
